oint $P(-1,0,1)$ where $t=\\pi $, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\pi )=\\frac{3}{5}\\,i-\\frac{4}{5}k,\\,N(\\pi )=-j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393792 1072 #uuid "0afd69e0-1da5-5a6a-895c-0f0f5cbf2711" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393792 1074 "First, notice that the position vector of the point $P(-1,0,1)$ is $r(\\pi )=-i+\\,k.$\n\nThe osculating plane passes through the point that is at the tip of the vector $r(1).$ The vectors $T(1)$ and $N(1)$ are parallel to this plane. Therefore, the equation of the plane (in parametric form) can be written as\n\n$$\nR(s,u)=r(\\pi )+s\\,T(\\pi )+u\\,N(\\pi ),\\,s,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the equation of the osculating plane at the point $(-1,0,1)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s,u) & =r(\\pi )+s\\,T(\\pi )+u\\,N(\\pi ) \\\\  & =(-i+\\,k)+s(\\frac{3}{5}\\,i-\\frac{4}{5}k)+u(-\\,j) \\\\  & =(-1+\\frac{3}{5}s)\\,i-u\\,j+(1-\\frac{4}{5}s)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393794 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393795 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393796 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393797 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393798 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393794 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393793 1080 #uuid "1aefb939-f80c-517f-8459-04195e8fbb29" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393794 1081 "R(s,u)=(-1+\\frac{3}{5}s)\\,i-u\\,j+(1-\\frac{4}{5}s)\\,k" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393794 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393794 1084 #uuid "734a6a1e-e685-50e7-b883-a6ebf4635869" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393795 1081 "R(s,u)=(5+3s)\\,i-5(u-1)\\,j+(5-4s)\\,k" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393795 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393795 1084 #uuid "2ab3dae2-3103-59c9-b9f5-5cbd28d86cc1" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393796 1081 "R(s,u)=(\\frac{3}{5}-s)\\,i-u\\,j+(\\frac{4}{5}+s)\\,k" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393796 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393796 1084 #uuid "f7703ddf-fee7-58ad-92ad-45013706727d" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393797 1081 "R(s,u)=(1+\\frac{3}{5}s)\\,i-(1+u)\\,j+(1-\\frac{4}{5}s)\\,k" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393797 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393797 1084 #uuid "3f9dae4c-d726-549b-acce-d5842fd2d48f" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393798 1081 "R(s,u)=(-1+3s)\\,i-\\,j+(1-4s)\\,k" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393798 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393798 1084 #uuid "7ae919b6-296b-5d05-a059-8fab72f07ffb" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393799 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393800 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393799 1069 "q-78242" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393799 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393799 1071 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -32\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393799 1072 #uuid "31ee87d6-9881-5423-8d44-047e84cf58fc" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393799 1074 "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -32\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =16\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =16v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=16v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=16.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393801 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393802 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393803 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393804 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393805 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393802 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393800 1080 #uuid "4f137406-87eb-59c2-9372-84d355135a99" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393801 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}16 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 16\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393801 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393801 1084 #uuid "80803840-34b8-5134-98b1-f302762ad086" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393802 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393802 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393802 1084 #uuid "d0f1ed27-08b7-59a4-bf54-c04cd4a88e2c" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393803 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 16 \\\\ 16 & 0\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393803 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533