186045585 true] [17592186393944 1084 #uuid "a9ccb688-6ce7-56f2-8a91-5c430e62080a" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393945 1081 "images/75/757072d5f7b2edaf1eb22e3e1a1c4135a387293396c9a4213ee3a2e213102ee6.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393945 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393945 1084 #uuid "b8c43a80-cb88-5719-a3f8-6293badb40f6" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393946 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393947 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393946 1069 "q-79571" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393946 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393946 1071 "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with light damped harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+41y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the damped oscillation?" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393946 1072 #uuid "5708124f-9743-5ab7-8b57-9c32436ebfac" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393946 1074 "The given equation represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. We are looking for solutions of the form $y={e}^{\\lambda t}.$\n\nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +41=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +41 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16)-16+41 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2} & =-25 \\\\ \\lambda +4 & =\\pm 5\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-4\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-4t}(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t).\n$$\n\nFrom the solution, the value of the angular frequency is $Ω=5\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}.$\n\nThe period of the damped oscillation $T$ is related to the angular frequency as follows:\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{Ω}\n$$\n\nSo the period is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{2\\pi }{5}\\,\\text{s}.\n$