194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393952 1084 #uuid "6cbb88df-1a01-5758-84f9-1948b1c83343" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393953 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393954 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393953 1069 "q-79620" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393953 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393953 1071 "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}+4t{y}^{′}+2y={e}^{t},\\,t>0\n$$\n\nhas the complimentary function ${y}_{c}(t)=\\frac{A}{t}+\\frac{B}{{t}^{2}}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(t)$ to this equation. \n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following result:* \n\n$$\n\\int t{e}^{t}\\text{d}t=(t-1){e}^{t}+C\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393953 1072 #uuid "1bb8ed71-56ab-536b-a7bf-0caa82667de7" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393953 1074 "First, we reduce the differential equation to the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(t){y}^{′}+Q(t)y=f(t).\n$$\n\nSo, we divide both sides of the given equation by ${t}^{2}.$ We get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{4}{t}{y}^{′}+\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}y=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe notice that the forcing term $f(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{t}.$ Additionally, we're given the fundamental solutions:\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(t)=\\frac{1}{t},\\,{y}_{2}(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the Wronskian:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{1}^{′}{y}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}{(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})}^{′}-{(\\frac{1}{t})}^{′}\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}(-\\frac{2}{{t}^{3}})-(-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{4}}+\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{4}}\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the Wronskian is not equal to zero, this confirms that the functions  ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ are independent. \n\nAccording to the method of variation of parameters, the particular solution of the differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}(t) & ={y}_{1}(t)u(t)+{y}_{2}(t)v(t),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =-\\int \\frac{f(t){y}_{2}(t)}{W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t={e}^{t}, \\\\ v(t) & =\\int \\frac{f(t){y}_{1}(t)}{W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})}\\,\\text{d}t=-\\int t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t=(1-t){e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}(t) & ={y}_{1}(t)u(t)+{y}_{2}(t)v(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\cdot (1-t){e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}{e}^{t}+(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}){e}^{t} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{t}+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{t}){e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393955 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393956 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393957 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393958 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1075 #edb/ref 17592186393959 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1079 #edb/ref 17592186393955 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393954 1080 #uuid "8de45fec-6d7a-5cbb-8c75-d5637ebdb1b3" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393955 1081 "{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}{e}^{t}" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393955 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393955 1084 #uuid "ea4d47ac-28b7-5cf4-9951-7b77a964f98a" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393956 1081 "{y}_{p}(t)=(\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{t}){e}^{t}" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186393956 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 tr