\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are $2$ pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. Now, from the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}={x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is a basis of the solution space of the system.\n\nFinally, we find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot (-1)+3\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{3}b \\\\  & =4b \\\\  & =4[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394141 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394142 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394143 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394144 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394145 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1079 #edb/ref 17592186394141 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394140 1080 #uuid "d253c50a-a61f-5f25-9a5a-b2a79e339ce2" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394141 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394141 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394141 1084 #uuid "fe651140-b