es formula in the form\n\n$$\n[\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 9}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -9 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394422 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394423 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394424 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394425 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394426 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1079 #edb/ref 17592186394423 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394421 1080 #uuid "e7cbaef8-14a8-5424-bff9-cdd4ca81b618" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394422 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394422 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] 