\\,x\\,]_{B}={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S}.\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is the matrix whose columns are the vectors of $B$ relative to the standard basis $S.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{S\\to B}$ from $S$ to $B.$ To do that, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}7 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-4)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute $[\\,x\\,]_{B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{B} & ={P}_{S\\to B}[\\,x\\,]_{S} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394429 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394430 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394431 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394432 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394433 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1079 #edb/ref 17592186394432 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394428 1080 #uuid "4dc08976-f574-52b6-a28f-57c50285b1e0" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394429 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394429 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394429 