ble negation:\n\n$$\nA∧(¬A∨¬¬B)≡A∧(¬A∨B)\n$$\n\n- Then, we use the distributive law (conjunction over disjunction):\n\n$$\nA∧(¬A∨B)≡(A∧¬A)∨(A∧B)\n$$\n\n- Next, we use the fact that the conjunction of a statement and its negation is a contradiction:\n\n$$\n(A∧¬A)∨(A∧B)≡c∨(A∧B)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the disjunction of a statement and a contradiction equals the original statement:\n\n$$\nc∨(A∧B)≡A∧B\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n¬[¬A∨(A∧¬B)]≡A∧B.\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394436 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394437 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394438 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394439 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394440 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1079 #edb/ref 17592186394438 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394435 1080 #uuid "91017620-b827-5673-acc6-2c29348ee517" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394436 1081 "\\text{c}" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394436 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394436 1084 #uuid "be689e1c-8de4-505b-b8d6-415931459c0b" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394437 1081 "A∨B" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394437 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394437 1084 #uuid "a4139a3f-cd05-511b-90bc-15e1ae8c8830" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394438 1081 "A∧B" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394438 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394438 1084 #uuid "a07e086a-f405-5c62-a9b0-9c054a955262" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] 