formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $2$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 2,\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 0}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394505 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394506 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394507 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394508 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394509 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1079 #edb/ref 17592186394509 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394504 1080 #uuid "eded17d8-4f57-5cb7-b32d-e7959dffa38a" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394505 1081 "{\\int }_{3\\pi /2}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394505 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394505 1084 #uuid "8cbf1a51-29f1-5394-92b0-8fa0f03ed53d" 13194139533465 17592186045585 tru