he orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394533 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394534 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394535 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394536 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394537 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1079 #edb/ref 17592186394535 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394532 1080 #uuid "0411b4e3-8abf-58a3-a87a-73efd9a201f1" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394533 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394533 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394533 1084 #uuid "da55d8b9-bcd7-5724-a71a-265e88540b54" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394534 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394534 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394534 1084 #uuid "d793713e-f4c6-5210-9cc9-12f75fc9f677" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394535 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394535 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394535 1084 #uuid "b41f91ae-46be-5eb5-91a3-b147826e5829" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394536 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394536 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394536 1084 #uuid "da4d25a6-e9cc-517d-b4e8-ca3772adec01" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394537 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394537 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394537 1084 #uuid "87fdcd3d-88e3-51ee-8bee-110ecb69fb31" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394538 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394539 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394538 1069 "q-83897" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394538 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394538 1071 "The growth rate of the hedgehog population $P(t)$ in a certain forest is jointly proportional to the hedgehog population at time $t,$ measured in years, and the difference between the forest's carrying capacity and the hedgehog population. The constant of proportionality is $0.000\\,005$ and the carrying capacity is $50\\,000.$ How many hedgehogs will there be in the forest after $20$ years given that there were $12\\,500$ hedgehogs initially? Round your answer to the nearest integer." 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394538 1072 #uuid "2763d23a-b642-55a2-bdf1-afa0ee05a7f3" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394538 1074 "Since the hedgehog population's growth rate is *jointly* proportional to the hedgehog population at time $t$ and the difference between the carrying capacity and the hedgehog population, the hedgehog population follows a logistic growth model.\n\nA logistic growth equation has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP(a-P),\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality, and $a>P$ is the carrying capacity.\n\nThe general solution to the logistic growth equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{a}{1+C{e}^{-akt}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the constant of proportionality is $k=0.000\\,005,$ and the carrying capacity is $a=50\\,000.$ Therefore, the hedgehog population growth is given by the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dP}{dt}=0.000\\,005P(50\\,000-P).\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{50\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-(50\\,000\\cdot 0.000\\,005)t}}=\\frac{50\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.25t}}.\n$$\n\nWe now substitute the initial condition $P(0)=12\\,500$ and solve for $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =12\\,500 \\\\ \\frac{50\\,000}{1+C{e}^{-0.25(0)}} & =12\\,500 \\\\ 1+C & =4 \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{50\\,000}{1+3{e}^{-0.25\\cdot t}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $t=20$ into the expression for $P(t),$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(20) & =\\frac{50\\,000}{1+3{e}^{-0.25\\cdot 20}} \\\\  & ≈49\\,009.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394540 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394541 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394542 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394543 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394544 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394539 1076 #