4 1072 #uuid "1a38eea7-13c5-59fe-a820-3f0859b3b4fd" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394674 1074 "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\overset{^}{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}54 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394676 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394677 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394678 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394675 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394