94709 1074 "To compute the arc length $L$ of a parametrically defined curve, we use the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x$ and $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)=2t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute these derivatives in the formula for arc length, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{(3{t}^{2})^{2}+(2t-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+4{t}^{2}-4t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394711 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394712 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394713 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394714 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394715 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1079 #edb/ref 17592186394715 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394710 1080 #uuid "f248aef5-8be7-5408-8afd-4afcb3aba568" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394711 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{9{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}-2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\," 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394711 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394711 1084 #uuid "8e2720b5-b7ef-506c-86d6-fa144d1dbad3" 13194139533465 17592