6394755 1081 "¬M∨(K∨L)" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394755 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394755 1084 #uuid "811aa8e6-a07e-5467-a2d7-93801d035f72" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394756 1081 "M∨(¬K∧¬L)" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394756 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394756 1084 #uuid "e5e73cc9-9a6c-5710-bb93-1712c8f7a500" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394757 1081 "¬M∨(K∧L)" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394757 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394757 1084 #uuid "5584d644-2138-505a-9f62-0cd34860d9e7" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394758 1068 #edb/ref 17592186394759 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394758 1069 "q-86846" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394758 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394758 1071 "Given the vector $x$ and the system of linear equations below, find the projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system.\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],\\,{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}-9{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394758 1072 #uuid "5cf24a3d-38a9-5fd8-a2a7-b75acfc0bac4" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394758 1074 "First, we need to find a basis for the solution space of the system. \n\nConsider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system, which we reduce to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 & -9 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is $1$ pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}$ are free variables. Now, from the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}.$ Therefore, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]={x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B={[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$ is the basis of the solution space of the system. \n\nNow, we find the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the solution space of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 10\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ -32\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ -32\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}42 \\\\ -70\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394760 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394759 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394761 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394759 1075 #edb/re