 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ is a free variable. From the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2}.$ Hence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, setting ${x}_{2}=3,$ we get the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖{v}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{13}.$ Dividing ${v}_{1}$ by its norm, we obtain the first column of $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{13}}{13} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{13}}{13}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394895 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394896 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394897 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394898 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1075 #edb/ref 17592186394899 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1079 #edb/ref 17592186394895 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394894 1080 #uuid "ca689d19-127e-5288-a0b5-11c9bff01ef0" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394895 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\sqrt{13}}{13} \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{13}}{13}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394895 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394895 1084 #uuid "262152dc-d095-58ad-b8fd-54192e4a8aa1" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394896 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186394896 1083 #edb/ref 175921860454