\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute $R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{11}\\cdot {r}_{12}=(\\frac{2}{3})\\cdot (-3)=-2.$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395115 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395116 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395117 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395118 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395119 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395119 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395114 1080 #uuid "eca9ce0b-73b4-529a-afb7-e8bec3879243" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395115 1081 "\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395115 