trix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables. On the other hand, from the first equation, we obtain ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}.$ \n\nHence, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nWe now deduce the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n- Since ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ we must have that ${x}_{2}=0$ and ${x}_{3}=1.$ As a result, $a=2(0)+1=1.$\n\n- Since ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}b \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],$ we must have that ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{3}=0.$ As a result, $b=2(1)+0=2.$\n\nTherefore, $a+b=1+2=3.$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395182 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395183 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395184 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395185 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395186 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395182 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395181 1080 #uuid "bb92e672-10a7-5664-a4ba-99167d7a01e6" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395182 1081 "3" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395182 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395182 1084 #uuid "8dabea23-d972-5617-9882-c14b15678f3e" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395183 1081 "2" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395183 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395183 1084 #uuid "3e6a69e2-80d1-5e2a-b545-4cab3ed2ec9d" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395184 1081 "0" 1319