n options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:\n\n  \n\n![](images/12/12c8be4491fe81d8ccf4ea964d883f2dc079f5183b72a8cd5b38260b8d3229d5.png)\n\nNote that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n   \n\n![](images/b3/b3dd1c29d770f36e4542427175eab7e102ee3e43a944d525459d28257e6d24a7.png)" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395522 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395523 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395524 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395525 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395526 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395523 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395521 1080 #uuid "d30dfba9-dad9-5198-8051-754b14711f5e" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395522 1081 "images/d0/d0abe9cb42672156fe48a934e1c9337af315d16d8afd75c8092ca9a01657e922.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395522 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395522 1084 #uuid "1f357254-f769-5436-bd0b-25358181a0f9" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395523 1081 "images/12/12c8be4491fe81d8ccf4ea964d883f2dc079f5183b72a8cd5b38260b8d3229d5.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395523 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395523 1084 #uuid "bed2a6a9-752e-5e4f-8000-ecbcb240a187" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395524 1081 "images/a1/a1e81bf264c71d1e4b14ea7a4f845c8276626e49238e10275afd9a1eeee22eec.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395524 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395524 1084 #uuid "f3c05222-2416-5b40-9ab2-a005052e8eca" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395525 1081 "images/b5/b54f31e2780f3f6c11ecc69eaab5dee59ddf2ba0c542f1e9bbee4f8fe25284ea.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395525 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395525 1084 #uuid "0447b677-359b-5b6f-a358-d3e5ef69c66d" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395526 1081 "images/a6/a6b83ae381ebc092e930f588b7ccd0851d09b521664285d700157c7091794fc2.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395526 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395526 1084 #uuid "bfabcff4-75db-540e-9198-01c700bc07c2" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395527 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395528 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395527 1069 "q-98527" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395527 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395527 1071 "Which of the following is the phase line of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{2}-12y-35?$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395527 1072 #uuid "796023e8-480d-5ead-996f-d9e2e236082e" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395527 1074 "To draw the phase line of the differential equation, we proceed using the following three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find the equilibrium solutions of the differential equation. \n\nIn this case, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2}-12y-35 & =0 \\\\ -({y}^{2}+12y+35) & =0 \\\\ -(y+7)(y+5) & =0 \\\\ y & =-7,-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium solutions are $y=-7$ and $y=-5.$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the intervals of $y$ for which $f(y)>0$ and $f(y)<0.$ \n\nConstructing a sign table, we get the following:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-7)$ | $(-7,-5)$ | $(-5,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-(y+7)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $y+5$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-7,-5),$ and negative for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-7)\\cup (-5,\\infty ).$\n\n**Step 3**: Draw the phase line using the following recipe:\n\n- Draw a vertical $y$-axis\n\n- Mark the equilibrium solutions\n\n- Draw arrows pointing up in the intervals where $f(y)>0$\n\n- Draw arrows pointing down in the intervals where $f(y)<0$\n\nApplying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.\n\n![](images/b0/b08c48590fe2538666e0e3a559c123b0f5cd3bb35680f2c98d3c14691780a575.png)" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395529 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395530 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395531 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395532 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395533 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395531 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395528 1080 #uuid "a5cb958b-c045-57d0-bdf5-09c3de6ac9b5" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395529 1081 "images/63/638f98960fbcfac5d0f10385037b92479fdab4177811f578d89bd997d7db2353.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395529 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395529 1084 #uuid "298e0721-a46f-5ceb-9c85-f931ed02acf8" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395530 1081 "images/7f/7f44aa29a8d99f144707d3126102ad633fd8b0f947ae16d862870444a5125793.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395530 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395530 1084 #uuid "1570cbd9-d5a9-51e5-9f83-3089fceb3038" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395531 1081 "images/b0/b08c48590fe2538666e0e3a559c123b0f5cd3bb35680f2c98d3c14691780a575.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395531 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395531 1084 #uuid "4b6a9b00-ac8c-5699-8ea3-9b92478b55f0" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395532 1081 "images/99/99e226354d8d1c48e11545d818083eb378ab931fd536e9a0389141e474ab27ee.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395532 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395532 1084 #uuid "e13e11d4-d69d-53ec-9487-a8851fd5e492" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395533 1081 "images/8d/8d7a4b4ac510e040a6d6ca87cf96e72c30a298ea450b0154d6080b9e73a19e8b.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395533 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395533 1084 #uuid "81174c62-81ee-55df-8611-d6e354b46ba6" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395534 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395535 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395534 1069 "q-98556" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395534 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395534 1071 "Which of the following is the phase line of the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{3}-4y?$" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395534 1072 #uuid "e4c26980-2b20-50dd-83dd-2c79a12fb753" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395534 1074 "To draw the phase line of the differential equation, we proceed using the following three steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find the equilibrium solutions of the differential equation. \n\nFirst, we factor the function $f(y),$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}-4y & =0 \\\\ y(y-2)(y+2) & =0 \\\\ y & =-2,0,2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium solutions are $y=-2,$ $y=0$ and $y=2.$\n\n**Step 2**: Find the intervals of $y$ for which $f(y)>0$ and $f(y)<0.$ \n\nIn this case, we have \n    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{3}-4y & >0 \\\\ y(y-2)(y+2) & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nConstructing a sign table, we get the following:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(-2,0)$ | $(0,2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y+2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $y$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $y-2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-2,0)\\cup (2,\\infty ),$ and negative for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (0,2).$\n\n**Step 3**: Draw the phase line using the following recipe:\n\n- Draw a vertical $y$-axis\n\n- Mark the equilibrium solutions\n\n- Draw arrows pointing up in the intervals where $f(y)>0$\n\n- Draw arrows pointing down in the intervals where $f(y)<0$\n\nApplying the above recipe, we get the following phase line for our differential equation.\n\n![](images/5f/5fa18a0300f34e5a471dac55a30a1edc838717ef154f3f776f6fabe08536a3e6.png)" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395536 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395537 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395538 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395539 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395540 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395537 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395535 1080 #uuid "27e889b3-4a89-5bdb-bd74-2ca245c80e34" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395536 1081 "images/66/66b90a2d1509ddb46e27d3e7164dbe1ab9b1f42aefd5df4b4482d8d2046f9bba.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395536 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395536 1084 #uuid "090719f1-8499-5e9d-b61c-1dab1a7eaab0" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395537 1081 "images/5f/5fa18a0300f34e5a471dac55a30a1edc838717ef154f3f776f6fabe08536a3e6.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395537 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395537 1084 #uuid "1d02280f-ba3e-552e-a757-4b2ff6d3e67c" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395538 1081 "images/fc/fca94bef82d6e693a93796fe353fc0efacbba86f6b51c59d1fe7df7932ffd912.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395538 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395538 1084 #uuid "37cf5aee-2a01-568a-ba64-446a635d03cc" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395539 1081 "images/7b/7b948fa43dc2f8a60f8e8df9d02ae65245891ae9ddb34ab8928b9dc696e36cc4.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395539 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395539 1084 #uuid "81e2da43-747e-5608-8968-53a516724969" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395540 1081 "images/a8/a8ee4e28944f944050c9378f62c72924219efb44e6b26c51f8a8ebc6b9300528.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395540 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395540 1084 #uuid "135b8596-5a73-574c-9298-ff3f4ad1bfc0" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395541 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395542 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395541 1069 "q-98709" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395541 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395541 1071 "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=-4$ and  $y=-1$ are equilibrium points\n\n- $y=-1$ is a source\n\n- $y=-4$ is a sink\n\nWhich of the following could be the phase line of the differential equation?" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395541 1072 #uuid "f792436d-ecaa-5cd1-8320-41fd8629919e" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395541 1074 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nLet's check each condition:\n\n- We're given that $y=-4$ and $y=-1$ are equilibrium points. We represent this on the phase line by drawing two distinct points at these locations.\n\n- We're given that $y=-1$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=-1$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=-4$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=-4$ (already drawn by the above property) and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\nTherefore, our phase line is as follows:\n\n![](images/8a/8a5f3a5965878cba364ee0e96af77bea41d53e6b2bd440340d72215e30db3a83.png)" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395543 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395544 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395545 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395546 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395547 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395546 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395542 1080 #uuid "fc2ee015-3e7a-59a7-81ea-733222e4b837" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395543 1081 "images/86/86978b5735f85962ae769e1781029b25b30b943ab274d29b93aee80521839c1f.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395543 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395543 1084 #uuid "0e5012c2-5230-5873-92a9-6488c8bfae5d" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395544 1081 "images/dd/dd7fd07ac56b96a71ff95444c99b21f3d862f8ab485495b501fea366fa15a8ab.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395544 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395544 1084 #uuid "8234414a-b377-5a1f-8fa0-ae1810f24c4c" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395545 1081 "images/82/82bb7d8cf05f050c733cb65632807ab14f290f57bdb033958759c54ccbb5f930.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395545 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395545 1084 #uuid "b6f5c1bb-8e32-515e-9bbd-0eb29aa53a5c" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395546 1081 "images/8a/8a5f3a5965878cba364ee0e96af77bea41d53e6b2bd440340d72215e30db3a83.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395546 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395546 1084 #uuid "eaf619c5-ca27-565a-85dd-948767c05061" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395547 1081 "images/8a/8af3fb742ff1ed334f8be319266dc2585d3c9675ec9fe959f77e165bfc7970c2.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395547 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395547 1084 #uuid "c9cc7a04-4036-5f92-b362-75351ff5d5d9" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395548 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395549 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395548 1069 "q-98781" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395548 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395548 1071 "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=-3$ is a sink\n\n- $y=0$ is a node\n\nWhich of the following could be the slope field of the differential equation?" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395548 1072 #uuid "55d1795f-d6ac-5ff7-a9de-20bb6292950d" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395548 1074 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $2$ equilibrium points, $y=-3$ and $y=0.$\n\n- We're given that $y=-3$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=-3$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=0$ is a node. This means that the arrows on either side of $y=0$ point in the same direction. Since the arrow just below $y=0$ points downward, the arrow just above it points downward too.\n\n![](images/db/db7e9ea076c3a1fe2cf5341b841693e36d5b9a9030e624da88d2cfd3b0d3a1b0.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](images/e4/e440928dfa83e3e653a2e508e9d01e53c73df84530402a393e82f56996eb5fde.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-3$ and $y=0.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-3$ appear to converge toward this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=0$ appear to diverge away from this line when we're looking below the line and appear to converge toward the line when we're looking above the line." 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395549 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395550 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395549 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395551 13194139533465 175921860455