with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](images/57/5737491c0a472a12cb3fd9e0b09cb5ede88b193a3f084ca89671e4669b945d5b.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-2$ and $y=3.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-2$ appear to diverge away from this line when we're looking above the line and appear to converge toward the line when we're looking below the line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=3$ appear to converge toward this line." 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395557 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395558 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395559 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395560 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395561 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1079 #edb/ref 17592186395557 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395556 1080 #uuid "0f774429-ecb7-569b-bb60-6fa8f2847a27" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395557 1081 "images/57/5737491c0a472a12cb3fd9e0b09cb5ede88b193a3f084ca89671e4669b945d5b.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395557 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395557 1084 #uuid "ff8dd8d0-7d50-5734-b6ea-496d2a570e8f" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395558 1081 "images/7d/7df58db225ecb32e6b51b2c16d78a557ca57e63f5d85551dfc1ddc85865e9ea4.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395558 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395558 1084 #uuid "d3cc9a9b-5ccf-500e-912e-e1f5b871939d" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395559 1081 "images/4e/4e360e24357a714978fdfb64b239381b3d7c66d13a1307c265f067881aaebc54.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395559 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395559 1084 #uuid "a7af3a60-0900-581d-aa3e-62e9b0e7848f" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395560 1081 "images/f1/f1302588da5388ebfa996005675625f98a9edee7c5ec0e99a2c897e70bd7e680.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395560 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395560 1084 #uuid "26e997a9-c909-5c38-8bf1-5444421cdf7c" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395561 1081 "images/a7/a7961c00b93091e3bf775f6f61f503d9f3d16ad30174c4f3310654f5aa75721c.png" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395561 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395561 1084 #uuid "3314cccf-cba5-50b7-a0ea-9fe1a2c4b4ab" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395562 1068 #edb/ref 17592186395563 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395562 1069 "q-98814" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395562 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395562 1071 "A particular autonomous differential equation has the following properties:\n\n- $y=-2$ is a sink\n\n- $y=-1$ is a source\n\n- $y=3$ is a node\n\nWhich of the following could be the slope field of the differential equation?" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395562 1072 #uuid "f2360fff-fd15-5336-bdf4-c3f68971846c" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395562 1074 "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nFirst, we draw the phase line with the given information. \n\nNote that there are $3$ equilibrium points, $y=-2,$ $y=-1,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- We're given that $y=-2$ is a sink. We represent this on the phase line by drawing a downward-pointing arrow just above $y=-2$ and an upward-pointing arrow just below it.\n\n- We're given that $y=-1$ is a source. We represent this on the phase line by drawing an upward-pointing arrow just above $y=-1$ and a downward-pointing arrow just below it  (already drawn by the above property).\n\n- We're given that $y=3$ is a node. This means that the arrows on either side of $y=3$ point in the same direction. Since the arrow just below $y=3$  points upward, the arrow just above it points upward too.\n\n![](images/6a/6a05aa0192d5edcb3181e44a5e3c15f5514372c8c50f105e9c4bbae40d660118.png)\n\nOf the given options, the only slope field that correspond with this phase line is the following:\n\n![](images/06/06a3d9118f9e3c09f374760a6e8209b33c9458e4d4b476c56fae3c57f2ca3fbe.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The slope field is horizontal at $y=-2,$ $y=-1,$ and $y=3.$\n\n- The slopes near $y=-2$ appear to converge toward this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=-1$ appear to diverge away from this line.\n\n- The slopes near $y=3$ appear to diverge away from this line when we're looking above the line and appear to converge toward the line when we're looking below the line." 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395563 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395564 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395563 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395565 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395563 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395566 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395563 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395567 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395563 1075 #edb/ref 17592186395568 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395563 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395563 1077 "selection" 13194139533465 17592186045585 true] [17592186395563 1079 #edb