begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-0,-(-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}),-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2},\\operatorname{sin}⁡t